## What got closed this session

**D-BAST-WRITEBACK-ABBA-DEADLOCK — FIXED AND VERIFIED.** `mxfs_dlm_bast_process` flushes at *two* sites; only site 2 (after `i_dlm_mode = NL`) can park a writeback submitter, because site 1 still nest-admits it. That's why three sessions of exercisers got "200/200 collisions" with zero demote-wait entries — they were colliding with the wrong flush. `tests/abba_wedge_ab.sh` now builds the cycle on demand; same-build A/B with matched exposure (21/21 site-2 entries, 10/10 blocked submitters) wedged with the fix off and passed with it on, and flipping the knob at runtime un-wedged a deadlocked node with exactly one `P25-IOEND-ADMIT req=3 src=writepages`. `fix27_shared_admit` now defaults on.

**D-CRASH-CONSISTENCY-32-BUDGET — resolved**, its stated dependency discharged.

## What I found, fixed, then had to walk back

A **new** permanent wedge on 3 of 32 quiesced nodes — caught by `node_responsive` only after I corrected it from a single `ps` snapshot (which measured load the script itself creates) to requiring the same PID still in D after a dwell. A demoter claim/cookie ring named the culprit outright: `bast_dwork_fn` overwrote and cleared `bast_work_fn`'s live `i_dlm_demoter`, stranding its trailing `xfs_irele`.

I made the claim un-stealable, marked it resolved — then found it **regressed `crash_consistency` from PASS 74s to FAIL at 90s**, proven by A/B against the pre-fix behaviour on one build. My earlier dismissal of that risk was wrong for a specific reason worth carrying forward: P73 prints every 10th wait (~30s), so it structurally cannot see individual 3s stalls. I reverted the entry to OPEN and revised the fix to two claim slots (both drains stay exempt, neither can strand the other), plus converted a third raw clobber site in `xfs_inode.c`. **That revision is built but not re-verified** — the rig went down before I could run it.

## Also advanced

- **D-UNMOUNT-BUSY-INODES**: the leaked reference is finally *named* (`xfs_lookup` at refcount level 1) via a grab-by-refcount-level table — the old 10-entry ring couldn't hold it, and a push/pop stack was measured wrong. Linked to the demoter clobber 3/3 vs 0/4. Kept OPEN: the mechanical chain isn't traced and the historical signature (775 regular files) differs from what I reproduced.
- **D-MOUNT-DEGRADES-WITH-USE**: reproduced and reframed — statfs and shared-dir cost are *unchanged*; what changes is a single-node straggler (77× spread). "Cumulative age" is retired.
- Refuted by measurement, so they don't get re-chased: P72 demoter override, EDEADLK self-clobber, cancelled-arm ref leak, PR-sweep growth.

